nodecode-covision is a rewrite of Covision-Consultants's Covision-Consultants/covision-agent-plugin:

  https://github.com/Covision-Consultants/covision-agent-plugin
  commit 373012bed0a36f7d4345a180eefc26352403cd3d
  Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) Covision-Consultants (LICENSE, whose appendix names no year or holder)

The rewritten plugin is the repository root of that commit. Its two halves are
kept. The MCP declaration (mcp.json) becomes the `covision' section's
endpoint, defaulting to the same production connector,
https://connector.covisionperformance.com/mcp; the cell speaks MCP's
Streamable HTTP transport to it -- initialize, the initialized notification,
tools/list and tools/call over JSON-RPC 2.0, the Mcp-Session-Id carried back,
a reply in a JSON body or in the last data: line of an event stream -- and
registers every tool the connector lists as a Nodecode tool under the
connector's own name, so the model calls the same approved read-only tools the
original's runtime would have listed. covision_tools lists them and
covision_call runs one by name, which is what the connector offers whether or
not the listing at start succeeded. The skill (skills/covision/SKILL.md) is
kept twice: its operating rules ride every request as a standing section, and
its use cases are the manual's page and the two tools' descriptions --
source facts apart from recommendations, the record's title, date or URL
cited, no claim that anything was written, a plain statement when access is
unavailable, and a focused follow-up when the request names no meeting,
organization or time range. /covision answers the connection the way the
original's setup notes answer `hermes mcp test`.

What was left out, and why: the browser OAuth sign-in. The original leaves it
to its runtime (`hermes mcp login`, whose pre-registered client and local
redirect port are its own), so the cell reads an access token from its section
and leaves the sign-in to the operator; a refresh still has to be re-pasted,
because the client id the token was issued to belongs to the client that
signed in. scripts/validate.mjs, the JSON-manifest check, has nothing to
check here: this cell's manifest is its .asd. LICENSE is the repository's
LICENSE, unchanged.
